-- the exchange of the two methyl groups, carrying their hydrogens with them. This preserves the bond
-- graph: nothing in the connectivity distinguishes the two methyls. It does not preserve the arrangement
-- at the beta carbon, which it reverses, so it is a symmetry of the graph and not of the configured
-- molecule — and that is the whole of why the two methyls of valine are diastereotopic.
vln-s : Vln → Vln
vln-s x = case x of
  vl-c1 → vl-c1
  vl-o1 → vl-o1
  vl-o2 → vl-o2
  vl-ho → vl-ho
  vl-ca → vl-ca
  vl-ha → vl-ha
  vl-n → vl-n
  vl-hn1 → vl-hn1
  vl-hn2 → vl-hn2
  vl-cb → vl-cb
  vl-hb → vl-hb
  vl-cg1 → vl-cg2
  vl-g11 → vl-g21
  vl-g12 → vl-g22
  vl-g13 → vl-g23
  vl-cg2 → vl-cg1
  vl-g21 → vl-g11
  vl-g22 → vl-g12
  vl-g23 → vl-g13
